        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2^{x+1}=16$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^{x+1}&=2^4\\\\x+1&=4\\\\x&=3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$3^{2x}=81$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3^{2x}&=3^4\\\\2x&=4\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q10-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$5^{x-1}<1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<1$",
          "worked": "Since $5>1$, the exponential function is increasing.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5^{x-1}&<5^0\\\\x-1&<0\\\\x&<1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q10-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$10^{\\frac13x}\\le1000$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le9$",
          "worked": "Since $10>1$, the exponential function is increasing.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}10^{x/3}&\\le10^3\\\\\\frac{x}{3}&\\le3\\\\x&\\le9\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q10-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{x-3}=8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^{-(x-3)}&=2^3\\\\-(x-3)&=3\\\\-x+3&=3\\\\x&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q10-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\left(\\frac1{10}\\right)^{5x}=\\frac1{10}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac15$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}10^{-5x}&=10^{-1}\\\\-5x&=-1\\\\x&=\\frac15\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q10-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$2^{x-2}<7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<2+\\log_2 7\\approx4.81$",
          "worked": "Since $2>1$, taking logarithms base $2$ preserves the inequality.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x-2&<\\log_2 7\\\\x&<2+\\log_2 7\\\\x&<2+\\frac{\\log_{10}7}{\\log_{10}2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe boundary is $2+\\log_2 7\\approx4.81$ to three significant figures.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q10-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$3^{x+5}>10$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x>\\log_3 10-5\\approx-2.90$",
          "worked": "Since $3>1$, taking logarithms base $3$ preserves the inequality.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+5&>\\log_3 10\\\\x&>\\log_3 10-5\\\\x&>\\frac{\\log_{10}10}{\\log_{10}3}-5\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe boundary is $\\log_3 10-5\\approx-2.90$ to three significant figures.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
